Method Example Use Case String literal <code>String s = "Hello"</code> Preferred, uses String Pool <code>new</code> keyword <code>new String("Hello")</code> Creates separate heap object From char array <code>new String(char[])</code> Convert char array From byte array <code>new String(byte[])</code> Convert bytes to text <code>valueOf()</code> <code>String.valueOf(123)</code> Convert any type to String <pre><code>// Preferred (String Pool)
String a = "Test";

// Creates duplicate object (avoid)
String b = new String("Test");

// a == b is FALSE (different objects)
// a.equals(b) is TRUE (same content)
</code></pre>
